#: ../../library/automation/workflows.rst:202
msgid ""
"A number of different Task types could be used in this phase. As long as "
"the Task is returning the required JSON array, the Task will work "
"correctly. Below is an example using a Groovy Task. This is simply "
"outputting a static payload though in a real world scenario you'd likely "
"use Task logic to output a dynamic array based on the Instance "
"configuration."
msgstr "A number of different Task types could be used in this phase. As long as the Task is returning the required JSON array, the Task will work correctly. Below is an example using a Groovy Task. This is simply outputting a static payload though in a real world scenario you'd likely use Task logic to output a dynamic array based on the Instance configuration."

#: ../../library/automation/workflows.rst:204
msgid ""
"def rtn = [\n"
"  priceData: [\n"
"    [\n"
"      incurCharges: 'always',\n"
"      currency: 'USD',\n"
"      unit: 'hour',\n"
"      cost: 2.0,\n"
"      price: 2.0\n"
"    ],\n"
"    [\n"
"      incurCharges: 'running',\n"
"      currency: 'USD',\n"
"      unit: 'hour',\n"
"      cost: 3.0,\n"
"      price: 3.0\n"
"    ],\n"
"    [\n"
"      incurCharges: 'stopped',\n"
"      currency: 'USD',\n"
"      unit: 'hour',\n"
"      cost: 1.0,\n"
"      price: 1.0\n"
"    ]\n"
"  ]\n"
"]\n"
"return rtn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/automation/workflows.rst:234
msgid "Nesting Workflows"
msgstr "Nesting Workflows"

#: ../../library/automation/workflows.rst:236
msgid ""
"|morpheus| allows Workflows to be nested for easier Workflow creation "
"when many Workflows are used in an environment which have only slight "
"differences or which are made up of common pieces. Nestable Workflows are"
" created like any other Operational Workflow. Once the Workflow is saved,"
" it can be embedded into a special Task type called \"Nested Workflow.\" "
"A Nested Workflow-type Task simply references an Operational Workflow "
"which may need to be used within other Workflows. Once Nested Workflow "
"Tasks are created they can be used as part of any new Operational or "
"Provisioning Workflows that are created thereafter (or may be added to "
"existing Workflows too). For more on creating Tasks, see |morpheus| `Task"
" documentation "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/automation/automation.html#tasks>`_."
msgstr "|morpheus| allows Workflows to be nested for easier Flujo de trabajo creation when many Workflows are used in an environment which have only slight differences or which are made up of common pieces. Nestable Workflows are created like any other Operational Flujo de trabajo. Once the Flujo de trabajo is saved, it can be embedded into a special Tarea type called \"Nested Flujo de trabajo.\" A Nested Flujo de trabajo-type Tarea simply references an Operational Flujo de trabajo which may need to be used within other Workflows. Once Nested Flujo de trabajo Tâches are created they peut ser used as part of any new Operational or Provisioning Workflows that are created thereafter (or may be added to existing Workflows too). For more on creating Tâches, see |morpheus| `Tarea documentation <https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/automation/automation.html#tasks>`_."

#: ../../library/automation/workflows.rst:238
msgid ""
"Results from prior Tasks are still accessed using the same syntax even "
"when a prior Task is embedded in a Nested Workflow. Additional syntax to "
"reference the Nested Workflow Task or the Workflow itself are not needed."
" See |morpheus| `Task documentation "
"<https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/automation/automation.html"
"#task-results>`_ for more on chaining Task results."
msgstr "Results from prior Tasks are still accessed using the same syntax even when a prior Task is embedded in a Nested Workflow. Additional syntax to reference the Nested Workflow Task or the Workflow itself are not needed. See |morpheus| `Task documentation <https://docs.morpheusdata.com/en/latest/library/automation/automation.html#task-results>`_ for more on chaining Task results."

